.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt AGED 8
.Os MidnightBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm aged
.Nd user age and date of birth tracking daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon manages a database of User IDs (UIDs) and their corresponding ages or
dates of birth. It provides a secure interface via a Unix Domain Socket
to allow applications to query the age range of the currently connected user.
.Pp
This is required in some jurisdictions for age verification.  For instance,
California law CA AB1043.
.Pp
The daemon is started by
.Pa root ,
runs as the
.Pa aged
user once its directories are set up,
and stores its data in a SQLite3 database located at
.Pa /var/db/aged/aged.db .
.Sh SECURITY
Access control is enforced using the
.Fn getpeereid
system call.
.Bl -bullet
.It
Only the
.Pa root
user (UID 0) is permitted to write or update records in the database.
.It
Non-root users may only query their own age range.
A request that names another UID is refused, and any other request is
answered for the caller's verified UID.
.It
The
.Pa root
user may query the age range of any UID, as it may also set it.
This lets a privileged program such as
.Xr mport 1 ,
run through
.Xr sudo 8 ,
check the user who ran it rather than
.Pa root .
.El
.Sh PROTOCOL
The daemon listens on a Unix Domain Socket at
.Pa /var/run/aged/aged.sock .
The socket is created with 666 permissions to allow all system users to
initiate a connection.
.Ss Writing Data (Root Only)
To store or update a user's information, send a string in the following format:
.Pp
.Dl "SET <uid> <type> <value>"
.Pp
Where
.Ar type
is either
.Ic age
or
.Ic dob .
.Ss Setting Region (Root Only)
To set the regulatory region, send a string in the following format:
.Pp
.Dl "REG <region>"
.Pp
Where
.Ar region
is one of the following valid values:
.Sy US-AL ,
.Sy US-CA ,
.Sy US-CO ,
.Sy US-IL ,
.Sy BR ,
.Sy US-NY ,
.Sy US-MI ,
.Sy US-WA ,
.Sy US-LA ,
.Sy US-UT ,
.Sy US-TX ,
.Sy US-FL ,
.Sy DE ,
.Sy EU ,
.Sy UK ,
.Sy AU ,
.Sy JP ,
.Sy null ,
or
.Sy parental .
.Pp
If the region is set to
.Sy US-CA ,
.Sy US-CO ,
.Sy US-IL ,
.Sy BR ,
or
.Sy parental ,
GET operations will return an age range. Any other value will cause GET
operations to return
.Sy -2,-2 .
.Ss Querying Data (All Users)
To query the age range of a user, send a string in the following format:
.Pp
.Dl "GET <uid>"
.Pp
The
.Pa root
user may name any UID.
Other users may only name their own; naming another UID, or a
.Ar uid
that is not a non-negative number, returns
.Sy ERR .
Any other data sent to the socket triggers a lookup for the caller's own UID.
If no age is recorded for a UID below 1000 (root and service accounts), it is
treated as 18.
The daemon returns a comma-delimited string representing the age range:
.Bl -tag -width "16,17XX" -compact
.It Sy "0,12"
Under 13 years of age.
.It Sy "13,15"
At least 13 and under 16.
.It Sy "16,17"
At least 16 and under 18.
.It Sy "18,-1"
18 years of age or older.
.It Sy "-1,-1"
Age is undefined or user not found.
.It Sy "-2,-2"
Age verification is not permitted in the configured region.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/aged/aged.sockXX" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/aged/aged.sock
Unix domain socket for communication.
.It Pa /var/db/aged/aged.db
SQLite3 database file.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getpeereid 2 ,
.Xr chmod 2 ,
.Xr sqlite3 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Lucas Holt Aq Mt luke@foolishgames.com
